WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:03.540
It only takes a tap on the brakes to start a traffic jam.

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:04.900
The next person brakes

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:07.660
and soon you have a shockwave of stop-and-go.

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:11.520
Similarly, anyone can help prevent them.

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:14.160
Just travel at a steady speed a safe distance

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:16.540
from the car ahead of you and avoid braking

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:17.630
unless necessary.

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:20.440
You’ll become a shock absorber in the system.

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:22.940
But most people don’t do this.

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:26.200
Artificial intelligence may be a solution.

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:29.240
Researchers showed that AI can learn to manage

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:32.940
traffic by controlling just a few autonomous vehicles.

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:38.120
They tested their system on figure-eights.

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:40.900
When the scientists replaced just one of the

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:43.760
14 “human”-driven cars with an AV

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:45.960
controlled by one of their algorithms,

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:48.540
average car speed doubled.

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:52.260
On ramps, replacing 10% of the cars

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:55.680
doubled the number of cars passing through.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:59.480
For bottlenecks, replacing 10% of the cars

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:02.960
increased throughput more than 20%.

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:07.260
In city grids where the AI controlled lights, not cars—

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:12.140
giving an algorithm control improved flow by 7%.

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:16.020
Until we have self-driving cars controlling traffic,

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:18.700
drivers can learn this from AI:

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:20.940
Keep your distance and brake less.

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:22.780
That’s smart driving.

